<section class="page-lead about-lead page-shell" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Field notes / 04 · About the organization</p>
  <h1 id="about-title">Build systems that hold up when <em>the easy path ends.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead-copy">ForgeWire Labs is an independent software engineering and research organization led by founder and principal engineer Jeremy Shows. The work ranges from distributed execution and agent systems to developer tools, local applications, and technical education.</p>
</section>

<section class="founder-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
  <div class="founder-label">
    <p class="eyebrow">Founder &amp; Principal Engineer</p>
    <h2 id="founder-title">Jeremy Shows</h2>
    <p>Engineering, research, and product direction</p>
  </div>
  <div class="founder-story">
    <p class="story-lede">Before building distributed systems and AI software, Jeremy worked as a mechanic, race-car builder, fabricator, IT professional, and small-business owner.</p>
    <p>That experience shaped a practical way of looking at software: understand the parts, how they connect, and what happens when one fails. A demo should meet limited hardware, changing requirements, and the moment an operator needs to step in.</p>
    <p>Jeremy leads research, architecture, implementation, debugging, testing, and documentation with substantial help from AI systems. He evaluates the results, chooses the direction, and decides what is accepted. The work also draws on open research, open-source software, commercial tools, and established engineering practice.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-principle" aria-labelledby="about-principle-title">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">A working rule</p>
    <h2 id="about-principle-title">Build it. Test it under failure.<br>Preserve the evidence. Understand its limits.</h2>
    <p>The public source is part of the engineering record. Where software is private or still in preview, the site says so.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="organization-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="organization-title">
  <div class="organization-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">One organization · Independent products</p>
    <h2 id="organization-title">One engineering practice. Each product keeps its own scope.</h2>
    <p>RepoPact, Anvil, SkillForge Academy, ForgeWire, and Fabric each have their own scope and maturity. ForgeLink is related work maintained under JeremyShows, with a separate repository and release channel. Cross-project references preserve those boundaries; each project has its own architecture and can be explored on its own.</p>
